---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn more about Hanzi."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-32 pb-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-balance font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-normal text-foreground mb-6">
        About Me
      </h1>
    </header>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg">
      <p>
        I'm <strong>Hanzi</strong>. I build tools that connect AI agents to the real world.
      </p>

      <p>
        Right now I'm working on <a href="https://browse.hanzilla.co">Hanzi Browse</a> — an open-source tool that gives AI coding agents a real browser. One setup command, and your agent can click, type, fill forms, and read authenticated pages in your actual Chrome with your existing logins. It works with Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and ten other agents.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before that I built <a href="https://skiplec.com">SkipLec</a>, an AI tool that turns lecture recordings into study notes, and <a href="https://jobs.hanzilla.co">jobs.hanzilla.co</a>, a job board for university students in Canada.
      </p>

      <p>
        I write about what I'm learning — growth, distribution, and the things nobody tells you about building products. You can read my posts on the <a href="/blog">blog</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in Touch</h2>

      <p>
        I'm always happy to talk about AI agents, browser automation, or startup stuff in general.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/hanzili">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hanzi-li-mcgill/">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/hanzi_li">X</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
